hadiths[32]{hadithnumber,text}:
"492","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""We are the last (of the nations) in order of appearance, but on the Day of Resurrection we will be the foremost in terms of reckoning and entering Paradise. Yes, the Jews and Christians were given the Book before us, and it was made obligatory upon them to worship on Friday, but they differed. So Allah guided us to it. Thus, all other people are behind us in this matter. The day of the Jews is tomorrow (Saturday), and the day of the Christians is the day after tomorrow (Sunday)."
"493","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is obligatory upon every adult to take a bath on Friday, to use the miswak, and to apply perfume if available."
"494","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ghusl on Friday like the ghusl of janabah (i.e., thoroughly), then goes (for the prayer), it is as if he has given a camel in charity. Whoever goes in the second hour, it is as if he has given a cow in charity. Whoever goes in the third hour, it is as if he has given a horned ram in charity. Whoever goes in the fourth hour, it is as if he has given a chicken in charity. Whoever goes in the fifth hour, it is as if he has given an egg in charity. When the Imam comes out (to deliver the sermon), the angels come to listen to the sermon (and the reward is no longer recorded)."
"495","Sayyiduna Salman al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes a bath on Friday, purifies himself as much as he can, then applies oil to his hair or uses the perfume of his house, then goes out (for the Friday prayer), and does not separate two people (sitting in the mosque), then prays as much as is written for him, then remains silent when the Imam delivers the sermon, his sins between this Friday and the previous Friday will be forgiven."
"496","Sayedna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) was asked that people say the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform ghusl (ritual bath) on Friday and wash your heads thoroughly, even if you are not in a state of janabah (major impurity), and use perfume."" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) replied that as for ghusl, yes (I also know that the Prophet, peace be upon him, commanded it), but as for perfume, I do not know."
"497","‘The Commander of the Faithful, Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), saw a silk garment being sold at the door of a mosque. He submitted, “O Messenger of Allah! If only you would buy this and wear it on Fridays and in the presence of delegations when they come to you.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Only that person will wear it who has no share in the Hereafter.” Afterwards, several garments of the same kind of silk came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he gave one silk garment to Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “O Messenger of Allah! You have given this to me, even though you had said something about the Hullah of Atarid.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “I did not give it to you so that you would wear it yourself.” So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave that garment to his polytheist brother who was in Makkah, and he wore it."
"498","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If I had not considered the hardship and difficulty for my Ummah, I would have surely commanded them to use the miswak at the time of every prayer."
"499","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that (on one occasion) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I have taught you a great deal about (the virtues of) the miswak."
"500","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite Alif Lam Meem As-Sajdah (Surah As-Sajdah) and (Hal Ata 'Alal Insani Hino Minad-Dahr) (Surah Ad-Dahr) in the Fajr (morning) prayer on Friday."
"501","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""All of you are guardians (i.e., rulers and responsible) and all of you will be questioned about your subjects. The Imam (leader) is a guardian and he will be questioned about his subjects, and a man is a guardian over the people of his house and he will be questioned about his subjects, and a woman is a guardian in her husband's house and she will be questioned about her and her subjects, and a servant is a guardian over his master's wealth and he will be questioned about it and his subjects."" (The narrator Ibn Shihab) says: I think he also said: ""A man is a guardian over his father's wealth and he will be questioned about his subjects, and all of you are guardians (i.e., rulers) and all of you will be questioned about your subjects."
"502","The narration of Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) in which it was mentioned that: ""In terms of sequence among nations, we are the last of all nations, but on the Day of Resurrection, in terms of reckoning and being taken to Paradise, we will be the foremost."" has already passed. (See the chapter: The Obligation of Jumu'ah...) At the end of this narration, it is further mentioned that then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is obligatory upon every Muslim to perform ghusl (ritual bath) once a week, on that day he should thoroughly clean his head and his body."
"503","`Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her)`, the respected wife of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), says that people used to come for the Friday prayer from their homes and from the surrounding villages of Madinah in turns. Due to dust, a lot of dust and sweat would accumulate on their bodies, and then sweat would also come out from their bodies, so there would be a bad smell. Then one of them came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) while he was with me, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""I wish you people would remain clean on this day (from dust and bad smell)."
"504","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that people used to do their work themselves, and when they went for Jumu'ah, they would go in that very state. So it was said to them: ""If only you would perform ghusl (ritual bath)."
"505","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to offer the Friday prayer after the sun had declined."
"506","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when it was very cold, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would offer the prayer early, and when it was very hot, he would delay the prayer until it became cooler, meaning the Friday prayer."
"507","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Abs (may Allah be pleased with him): And he was going for the Friday prayer at that time, that I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever's both feet become dusty in the way of Allah, Allah has made the (Hell) fire forbidden for him (i.e., the fire of Hell cannot touch him)."
"508","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that: ""No person should make his brother get up from his place and then sit in his place himself."" It was asked, ""Is this only for Friday?"" He replied, ""For Friday and for other occasions as well."
"509","Sayyiduna Sa’ib bin Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) says that on the day of Jumu’ah, the adhan during the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and during the era of the Commander of the Faithful Abu Bakr as-Siddiq and ‘Umar al-Faruq (may Allah be pleased with them both), used to be given when the Imam sat on the pulpit. Then ‘Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) became the Caliph and (the number of) Muslims increased, so ‘Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) added a third adhan at Zawra. (Imam Bukhari, may Allah have mercy on him, said that Zawra is the name of a place in the market of Madinah.)"
"510","Sayyiduna Sa’ib bin Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) in another narration says that during the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) there was only one mu’adhdhin, and on the day of Jumu’ah he would give the adhan only when the imam sat down, that is, when he sat on his pulpit."
"511","Narrated from Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was sitting on the pulpit when the muezzin gave the call to prayer. When he said (Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar), Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) also said (Allahu Akbar Allahu Akbar). Then the muezzin said ((Ashhadu an la ilaha illallah)), so Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said ((Wa ana)). The muezzin said ((Ashhadu anna Muhammadur Rasulullah)), so Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said ((Wa ana)). When the call to prayer was finished, Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O people! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at this very place (i.e., the pulpit) that when the muezzin gave the call to prayer, he (peace be upon him) would say just as you have heard me say."
"512","The hadith of Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the pulpit has already been mentioned (see the Book: Description of Prayer... Chapter: Performing prayer on roofs, pulpits, and wooden platforms) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on top of it (the pulpit) and then stepped down backwards. In this narration, it is further mentioned that when he finished, he turned to the people and said: “O people! I did this so that you may follow me and learn my (method of) prayer.”"
"513","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): There was a trunk of a date-palm tree which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand by (while delivering the sermon). When a pulpit was placed for him, we heard a sound from that trunk like the crying of a pregnant she-camel for ten months, until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down from the pulpit and placed his hand on the trunk. (Then the sound stopped.)"
"514","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the sermon while standing, then he would sit down, then stand up again, just as you do now."
"515","Sayyiduna Amr bin Taghlib (may Allah be pleased with him) says that some wealth or something was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he (peace be upon him) distributed it. He gave to some people and did not give to others. Then news reached him (peace be upon him) that those whom he had not given were displeased. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) praised and glorified Allah, then said: ""To proceed! By Allah, I give to some and leave others, even though the one whom I leave is more beloved to me than the one to whom I give. But I give to some people because I see restlessness and anxiety in their hearts. (And those whom I do not give), I entrust them to the contentment and goodness that Allah has placed in their hearts. Among such people is Amr bin Taghlib (may Allah be pleased with him)."" (Amr bin Taghlib [may Allah be pleased with him] says:) By Allah! I do not wish to have even red camels in exchange for this statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"516","`Sayyiduna Abu Humayd Sa'idi (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up one night after the prayer and recited the Tashahhud and praised Allah as He deserves to be praised, then said, ""Amma ba'd!."
"517","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that (one day) the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit, and it was the last gathering in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a large cloak draped over his shoulders and had tied his blessed head with a dusty-colored band. Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O people! Come near to me."" So the people gathered close to him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). After that, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""To proceed! This tribe of Ansar will keep decreasing, and other people will keep increasing. Therefore, whoever among the Ummah possesses anything and has the authority by which he can harm or benefit someone, he should accept the good deeds of the righteous among them (i.e., the Ansar) and overlook the mistakes of the wrongdoers among them."
"518","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): A man came (to the mosque) while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon, and sat down. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him: ""Have you prayed two rak'ahs (Tahiyyat al-Masjid)?"" He replied: ""No."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Get up and pray two rak'ahs."
"519","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` (on one occasion) during the time of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), people were afflicted with drought. On a Friday, while the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was delivering the sermon, a Bedouin stood up and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Wealth has been destroyed and children are hungry, so pray (to Allah) for rain for us."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised both his hands, and at that time we did not see even a patch of cloud in the sky. But by the One in Whose hand is my soul, he (peace and blessings be upon him) had not yet lowered his hands when clouds gathered like mountains. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not descend from his pulpit until I saw rain dripping from his blessed beard. Then it rained upon us that day, and the next day, and the third day, and the fourth day, and so on until the next Friday. Then that same Bedouin (or Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said) or another man stood up during the Friday (sermon) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! (Due to the abundance of rain) houses have collapsed and wealth has been submerged, so pray to Allah for us."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) raised both his hands and said: ""O Allah! Let the rain fall around us and not upon us."" Then whichever direction the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed to a cloud, it would move away, and the whole of Madinah became clear like a basin, and the stream of the valley of Qanat flowed for a month, and whoever came from any direction would describe the state of the rain."
"520","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If, on the day of Jumu'ah, while the Imam is delivering the sermon, you say to your companion, 'Be quiet,' then surely you have engaged in idle talk."
"521","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the day of Friday and said: ""There is a moment in it such that if a Muslim servant encounters it while standing and praying, and asks Allah for something, Allah will surely grant him that thing."" And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) indicated with his hand to show the brevity of that moment."
"522","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): We were offering prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a caravan (from Syria) arrived carrying grain. The people turned towards the caravan until only twelve men remained with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then this verse was revealed: ""And when they saw a transaction or a diversion, they rushed to it and left you standing (O Prophet) in the sermon."" (__QUR_N__ Al-Jumu'ah: 11)"
"523","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to offer two rak'ahs before Zuhr and two rak'ahs after Zuhr, and two rak'ahs after Maghrib in his house, and (also) two rak'ahs after Isha, and he would not offer (these) after Jumu'ah until he returned (to his house), then he would offer two rak'ahs."
